<title>USA: U.S. copper production, inventory rise in October.</title>
<headline>U.S. copper production, inventory rise in October.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. refined copper production rose to 185,900 short tons in October - its highest for the year - compared to 161,500 tons in September and 164,900 tons in October 1995, the American Bureau of Metal Statistics reported.</p>
<p>Refined deliveries in October totaled 189,500 tons, down from a revised 193,700 tons in September and 177,400 tons in October 1995.</p>
<p>Refined inventories were 71,100 tons in October, their highest level for the year, and up from 65,500 tons in September. Inventories in October last year were 46,800 tons.</p>
<p>((New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
